From 97327c74db30dc85c40e404ec68b4322e0fd43fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <05jeelo30@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:24:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: Drop the codec2 vendor0_software service label

The onyx device tree already labels
android.hardware.media.c2.IComponentStore/vendor0_software, and a second
identical entry in service_contexts breaks the sepolicy build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QY97AsgNLyAwQpzrsxC9zt
---
 sepolicy/vendor/service_contexts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/service_contexts b/sepolicy/vendor/service_contexts
index 223d413..7788809 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/service_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/service_contexts
@@ -2,5 +2,3 @@
 vendor.xiaomi.hardware.misys    u:object_r:misys_service:s0
 vendor.xiaomi.hardware.misys.common.IMiSysImpl/default    u:object_r:hal_misys_vendor_service:s0
 vendor.xiaomi.hardware.misys.common.IHypSysIntl/default   u:object_r:hal_misys_vendor_service:s0
-# Without this the store falls through to the neverallowed default_android_service catch-all
-android.hardware.media.c2.IComponentStore/vendor0_software    u:object_r:hal_codec2_service:s0
-- 
2.43.0

